on, or the Bank of Guyana\", \"provenance\" \"https://gra.gov.gy/how-to-obtain-a-tin/\", \"owner-authority\" \"Guyana Revenue Authority (GRA)\"}, \"rep\" {\"provenance\" \"https://guyanachronicle.com/2016/04/29/the-public-procurement-commission/\", \"owner-authority\" \"Public Procurement Commission (PPC)\", \"legal-basis\" \"Constitutional basis: Article 212W of the Constitution of Guyana. First Commissioners sworn in 28 October 2016. The PPC is the oversight body a debarment/registry decision under the Procurement Act ultimately answers to.\"}, \"business-registration\" {\"provenance\" \"https://dcra.gov.gy/ ; https://www.grantthornton.gy/publications/guyanese-registration-requirements-for-non-resident-companies/\", \"legal-basis\" \"Deeds and Commercial Registries Authority Act No. 4 of 2013 (establishes DCRA; administers the Companies Act, the Business Names (Registration) Act, and the Partnership Act). A NON-RESIDENT company must register under the Companies Act 1991 when 'carrying on an undertaking' in Guyana -- triggered by ANY of: maintaining an office; maintaining a share transfer/registration office; entering two or more contracts with local parties for work performed in Guyana; appointing a resident agent; or owning/using profit-generating assets in Guyana. No online registration platform -- physical registration with the Registrar of Companies is required.\", \"owner-authority\" \"Deeds and Commercial Registries Authority (DCRA)\"}}", :permit/jurisdiction "GUY", :source/dataset "permits", :permit/provenance ["https://www.npta.gov.gy/procurement-documents/procurement-act-and-regulations/"], :permit/authority "National Procurement and Tender Administration (NPTA)", :permit/subject-key "GUY", :permit/subject-name "Guyana", :permit/national-spec "Register of Bidders registration under the Procurement Regulations 2004 / Procurement Amendment Regulations 2016 / Regulations No. 23 of 2022 (Register of Bidders); centralized e-procurement portal eprocure.gov.gy (